				</LookAt>
				<styleUrl>#__managed_style_030E64063A41CCEEBB8C</styleUrl>
				<Placemark id="08E238054524F0F3DA3B">
					<name>Kamiak Bench North</name>
					<description><![CDATA[<div>Cool little bench structure great for unusual under bars and other flow.&nbsp;<br></div><div><br></div><div>A long series of circular bike racks near a brick wall are great for rail strides, plyos,&nbsp; wall/rail tacks, over/under, ect...<br></div><div><br></div><div>There are some interesting challenges to be had with some rocks and a small tree in the NW corner.&nbsp;<br></div><div><br></div><div>There is a wall to wall running pre on the south side near the doors. Same distance as the southern bench area, but with about a foot of height advantage (or disadvantage if you're keen).&nbsp;<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The awning over the doorways is very climbable, and can get you onto the roof of the north buildings.&nbsp;🤫 However there are security cameras everywhere. It's not clear if these cameras are continuously monitored.<br></div>]]></description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>-122.3024340129694</longitude>
						<latitude>47.90176161149563</latitude>
						<altitude>150.5330046047955</altitude>
						<heading>144.1346860816143</heading>
						<tilt>56.43492548668024</tilt>
						<gx:fovy>34.99999999997837</gx:fovy>
						<range>141.2507338710566</range>
						<altitudeMode>absolute</altitudeMode>
					</LookAt>
					<styleUrl>#__managed_style_3E6E43670441CCEEBB90</styleUrl>
					<Polygon>
						<outerBoundaryIs>
							<LinearRing>
								<coordinates>
									-122.3025550472685,47.90156569888107,147.929351989673 -122.3022711641141,47.90156668776062,148.2247149533015 -122.3022718332884,47.9016385953666,148.4348989335624 -122.3022284185003,47.90164411795101,148.2920752602742 -122.3022475536672,47.90198463588075,148.1119847134379 -122.3023544097539,47.9019878823165,147.8812964925064 -122.3023636752911,47.90190771075888,147.9692612114028 -122.3024931661264,47.90191358606832,147.8392104140651 -122.3025568650217,47.90191699873199,147.8257286889244 -122.3025550472685,47.90156569888107,147.929351989673 
								</coordinates>
							</LinearRing>
						</outerBoundaryIs>
					</Polygon>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark id="063989BD0C24FFBACC4A">
					<name>North Entrance Mini-Gap</name>
					<description><![CDATA[<div>A very forgiving mini-gap between two low concrete dividers. The distance between the dividers is about 9ft. On one side, there is about a 3-4 ft drop between dividers, and on the other, only a few inches. Since the jump is otherwise identical, the low-drop side is a perfect prep. The dividers are at least 3ft across on top, making them forgiving on overshoots, and allowing small gather steps.&nbsp;<br></div>]]></description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>-122.3019169098567</longitude>
						<latitude>47.90100133774482</latitude>
						<altitude>151.256611415561</altitude>
						<heading>178.7128553633564</heading>
						<tilt>56.34377447171484</tilt>
						<gx:fovy>35</gx:fovy>
						<range>39.78500986262589</range>
						<altitudeMode>absolute</altitudeMode>
					</LookAt>
					<styleUrl>#__managed_style_193905038041CCEEBB8C</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>-122.3019314878615,47.90099212848467,149.7668035254094</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark id="085C671C8C24F0EBE2E0">
					<name>Kamiak High School Back Patio</name>
					<description><![CDATA[<div>Small local spot. Never hosted a large group AFAIK. A few small walls, picnic tables, and non-ideal rails.&nbsp;<br></div>]]></description>
